1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:07,500
You sure are...

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,290
a member of what? Bert the Turtle? Just good friends, because every one of us must

3
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:14,860
remember to do the same thing. That's what this film is all about.

4
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:21,160
Duck and Cover. This is an official civil defense film produced in cooperation with the

5
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:22,930
Federal Civil Defense Administration

6
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:26,620
and in consultation with the Safety Commission of the National Education

7
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:30,800
Association, produced by Archer Productions Incorporated.

8
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:38,890
Meet all these nice people. Bert the Turtle. I really can't blame you.

9
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:43,690
You see, Bert is a very, very careful fella, and he's in danger.

10
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:49,400
This is the way he keeps from being hurt. Sometimes it even saves his life.

11
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:53,210
That's why these children are practicing to duck

12
00:00:53,210 --> 00:00:55,570
and cover, just as you do in your school.

13
00:00:56,790 --> 00:01:00,010
We all know the atomic bomb is very dangerous.

14
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:04,290
Since it may be used against us, we must get ready for it, just as we are ready for

15
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:08,780
many other dangers that are around us all the time. Fire is a danger.

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,320
It can burn whole buildings if someone is careless. But we are ready for fire.

17
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:17,760
We have a fine fire department to put out the fire.

18
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:21,420
And you have fire drills in your school. So you know what to do.

19
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:27,550
We know it can be dangerous, and sometimes it causes bad accidents. We already...

20
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,590
have safety rules that car drivers and people who are walking must obey.

21
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:36,640
Now we must be ready for a new danger. The atomic bomb.

22
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:41,620
First, you have to know what happens when an atomic bomb explodes.

23
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:46,180
You will know when it comes. We hope it never comes. But when it does...

24
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:51,180
it looks something like this. There is a bright flash, brighter than the sun, brighter

25
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:56,000
than anything you've ever seen. If you are not ready and do not know what to do...

26
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:00,930
It could hurt you in different ways. It could knock you down hard

27
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:05,130
or throw you against a tree or a wall. It is such a big explosion.

28
00:02:05,750 --> 00:02:08,690
It can smash in buildings and knock signboards over

29
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:12,310
and break windows all over town. But if you duck

30
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:19,310
and cover, like Bert, you will be much safer. If you know how bad sunburn can feel, the

31
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:23,010
atomic bomb flash could burn you worse than a terrible sunburn.

32
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,890
Especially when you are not covered.

33
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,400
Now, you

34
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:30,640
and I don't have shells to crawl into like Bert the Turtle. All we have to do is cover

35
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:35,540
up, in our own way: first duck, and then cover.

36
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:38,740
And very tightly. You cover the back of your neck.

37
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:43,580
If your face, duck and cover underneath the table or desk

38
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,220
or anything else close by.
